                  "from": 110.655,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2911907,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Well, the eucalyptus tree is an important tree for lots of reasons.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 116.0,
                  "from": 111.200005,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2911920,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "For example, it gives shelter to creatures like birds and bats, and these and other species also depend on it for food, particularly the nectar from its flowers. So it supports biodiversity. It's useful to us humans too because we can kill germs with a disinfectant made from oil extracted from eucalyptus leaves. The eucalyptus grows all over Australia, and the trees can live for up to four hundred years. So it's alarming that all across the country, numbers of eucalyptus are falling because the trees are dying off prematurely.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2911921,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For example, it gives shelter to creatures like birds and bats, and these and other species also depend on it for food, particularly the nectar from its flowers.",
